#### **2. Mathematical Formulation: Inverse Cubic Gravity Calculation**

```cpp
class CelestialBody {
public:
    Vec3 position; // 3D coordinates
    float mass;     // Mass of the celestial body
    float gravitational_constant = 6.674e-11; // Standardized constant

    // Calculate gravitational force between two objects
    Vec3 calculateGravitationalForce(CelestialBody& otherBody) const {
        float distance = length(position - otherBody.position);
        float force_magnitude = (gravitational_constant * mass * otherBody.mass) / pow(distance, 3);

        // Return force vector pointing toward the other body
        return normalize(position - otherBody.position) * force_magnitude;
    }
};
```

